  "term": "diffusion tensor imaging",
  "definition": "Diffusion tensor imaging is a form of diffusion-weighted MRI that tracks how water moves in three dimensions. It is mainly used to visualize the brain’s white matter by showing the direction, location, and degree of organization of neural tracts, which can reveal small structural differences or changes linked to disease or treatment.",
